import AxQM.Concrete.DeutschCompressedReachable
import AxQM.Concrete.DeutschReachableCircuits

/-!
# Concrete: universality of the Deutsch gate with ancillas — compressed `G`-placement circuits
dense in `U(2ⁿ)` up to phase (matrix level, N&C Ex 4.44)

Every statement is about matrices: the multiply-controlled single-qubit wire gate
`mcCtrlSingleQubit`, the reversible gates `IsToffoliPermGate`, the coordinate-subspace compression
`compress`, the reachable-circuit submonoids `deutschDataReachableCircuits` /
`deutschReachableCircuits`, and the register-layout equivalences of
`Concrete/RegisterCompressionBridge.lean`.

## Universality *with ancillas*

`Concrete/DeutschCompressedReachable.lean` collected the `G`-placement circuits that preserve the
ancilla-`|1⟩` subspace into a submonoid `M` (`deutschAncillaReachableCircuits`) and compressed it to
the data-register submonoid `Ncomp` (`deutschDataReachableCircuits`, `= compress ι '' M`), then
showed the **single-qubit** generators of the universality density core lie in `Ncomp`
(`singleQubitOnWire_mem_deutschDataReachableCircuits`). This file supplies the
**reversible** generators and concludes the matrix-level universality statement.

* **The reversible gates (`IsToffoliPermGate`) as compressed `G`-placements.** The density core's
  abstract gate set `deutschReachableGateSet dataEnc α` also contains the `≤ 2`-control reversible
  gates `IsToffoliPermGate dataEnc N` — a `Toffoli`/`CNOT`/`NOT` on the data register. Each is
  realised from `G` by placing the Pauli-`X` orbit member on a data target wire with the Deutsch
  gate's **two** control wires assigned as follows: the `|C| ≤ 2` data controls of the gate go on
  data wires, and the remaining `2 - |C|` controls go on ancilla wires held `|1⟩`. Holding a control
  at `|1⟩` makes it transparent (`forall_mem_regExtend_eq_one_iff`), so a `Toffoli` `C²(X)` placed
  with `k` controls on ancillas acts as the reduced `C^{2-k}(X)` on the data wires — exactly N&C's
  realisation of the lower-arity reversible gates from a Toffoli. The placement is a genuine
  two-control `G`-placement (`exists_control_pair_descend_of_card_le_two` produces **distinct**
  control wires), its compression is `IsToffoliPermGate dataEnc N`
  (`isToffoliPermGate_compress_mcCtrlSingleQubit_pauliX`), and it is reachable
  (`mcCtrlSingleQubit_pauliX_mem_closure_deutschWirePlacedReachable`).

* **The density transfer.** With both halves of `deutschReachableGateSet dataEnc α` inside `Ncomp`,
  the abstract reachable-circuit submonoid `deutschReachableCircuits dataEnc α` (generated by that
  gate set) is `≤ Ncomp` (`Submonoid.closure_le`), so its topological closure is contained in that
  of `Ncomp` (`closure_mono`). Transporting the abstract density core
  `exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschReachableCircuits` along that containment gives the
  **matrix-level universality of `G` with ancillas**: the data-register actions of `G`-placement
  circuits are dense in `U(2ⁿ)` up to a global phase, for `α` irrational.

Every reachable gate is realised as a compressed *actual* `G`-placement circuit; no abstract gate
is assumed.

## The construction and results

Fix a full-register encoding `fullEnc`, a data-register encoding `dataEnc`, a wire-splitting
`e : Fin M ≃ Fin m ⊕ Fin n` (data wires `Sum.inl`, ancilla wires `Sum.inr`), and two distinct
ancilla wires `a₀ ≠ a₁`.

* `exists_control_pair_descend_of_card_le_two` — for `≤ 2` data controls `C`, two **distinct**
  full-register control wires whose control condition descends, on the ancilla-`|1⟩` subspace, to
  the data control condition over `C`: the `|C|` data controls sit on data wires, the rest on
  ancillas.
* `isToffoliPermGate_mem_deutschDataReachableCircuits` — **the reversible realisation** (`α`
  irrational): every `IsToffoliPermGate dataEnc N` lies in `deutschDataReachableCircuits` — it is
  the data-register action of a Pauli-`X` `G`-placement with its `≤ 2` data controls padded to
  `G`'s two controls by ancillas held `|1⟩`.
* `exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschDataReachableCircuits` — **the matrix headline** (`α`
  irrational, `m ≥ 1`): for any `U ∈ U(2ⁿ)` some global phase `e^{ia}` makes `e^{ia} • U` a limit of
  `deutschDataReachableCircuits` — the compressed `G`-placement circuits are dense in `U(2ⁿ)` up to
  a global phase. Universality of `G` with ancillas, at the matrix level.
-/

namespace AxQM.Concrete

open Matrix

variable {M m n D d : ℕ} (fullEnc : (Fin M → Fin 2) ≃ Fin D)
  (dataEnc : (Fin m → Fin 2) ≃ Fin d) (e : Fin M ≃ Fin m ⊕ Fin n)

/-- **Two distinct full-register control wires realising `≤ 2` data controls.** Given data controls
`C` with `C.card ≤ 2` and two distinct ancilla wires `a₀ ≠ a₁`, there are two **distinct**
full-register wires `a, b` whose control condition descends, on the ancilla-`|1⟩` subspace, to the
data control condition over `C`: for every data bit `c`, `c ∈ C ↔ e.symm (Sum.inl c) ∈ {a, b}`.

The `|C|` data controls of `C` go on data wires `e.symm (Sum.inl c)`; the remaining `2 - |C|`
controls go on ancilla wires `e.symm (Sum.inr aᵢ)` — held `|1⟩`, hence transparent, so they do not
contribute to the descended condition. The distinctness `a ≠ b` certifies that the resulting
placement is a genuine **two-control** `G`-placement (not a degenerate single-control gate). Proved
by `Finset.card_eq_{zero,one,two}` on `C.card ∈ {0, 1, 2}`; distinctness comes from the injectivity
of `e.symm` together with `a₀ ≠ a₁` (`|C| = 0`), `Sum.inl ≠ Sum.inr` (`|C| = 1`), and the two data
controls being distinct (`|C| = 2`). -/
theorem exists_control_pair_descend_of_card_le_two (a₀ a₁ : Fin n) (ha : a₀ ≠ a₁)
    {C : Finset (Fin m)} (hcard : C.card ≤ 2) :
    ∃ a b : Fin M, a ≠ b ∧
      ∀ c : Fin m, c ∈ C ↔ e.symm (Sum.inl c) ∈ ({a, b} : Finset (Fin M)) := by
  have hcard3 : C.card = 0 ∨ C.card = 1 ∨ C.card = 2 := by omega
  rcases hcard3 with h | h | h
  · rw [Finset.card_eq_zero] at h
    subst h
    refine ⟨e.symm (Sum.inr a₀), e.symm (Sum.inr a₁), fun hab => ?_, fun c => ?_⟩
    · exact ha (Sum.inr_injective (e.symm.injective hab))
    · simp [e.symm.injective.eq_iff]
  · rw [Finset.card_eq_one] at h
    obtain ⟨c₀, h⟩ := h
    subst h
    refine ⟨e.symm (Sum.inl c₀), e.symm (Sum.inr a₀), fun hab => ?_, fun c => ?_⟩
    · exact Sum.inl_ne_inr (e.symm.injective hab)
    · simp [e.symm.injective.eq_iff]
  · rw [Finset.card_eq_two] at h
    obtain ⟨c₀, c₁, hne, h⟩ := h
    subst h
    refine ⟨e.symm (Sum.inl c₀), e.symm (Sum.inl c₁), fun hab => ?_, fun c => ?_⟩
    · exact hne (Sum.inl_injective (e.symm.injective hab))
    · simp [e.symm.injective.eq_iff]

/-- **The reversible gates `Toffoli`/`CNOT`/`NOT` are compressed `G`-placements** (Nielsen & Chuang,
Exercise 4.44, reversible half). When `α` is irrational, every `≤ 2`-control reversible gate
`IsToffoliPermGate dataEnc N` lies in `deutschDataReachableCircuits` — it is the data-register
action of a `G`-placement circuit with the ancillas held `|1⟩`.

Unfolding `IsToffoliPermGate` gives `N = permGate dataEnc (mcNotPerm C ht)` with `t ∉ C` and
`C.card ≤ 2`. Choose two distinct control wires `a, b` descending to `C`
(`exists_control_pair_descend_of_card_le_two`) and place the Pauli-`X` orbit member on the data
target wire `e.symm (Sum.inl t)` with controls `{a, b}`. That placement is a data-target gate (hence
ancilla-preserving, `mcCtrlSingleQubit_dataTarget_mem_compressionInvariant`) and a genuine
two-control `G`-placement, reachable from `G`
(`mcCtrlSingleQubit_pauliX_mem_closure_deutschWirePlacedReachable`), so it is a member of `M`; its
compression is
`mcCtrlSingleQubit dataEnc C t pauliX = permGate dataEnc (mcNotPerm C ht) = N`
(`compress_mcCtrlSingleQubit_dataTarget_of_ctrl_iff` with the descent from
`forall_mem_regExtend_eq_one_iff`, then `mcCtrlSingleQubit_pauliX_eq_permGate`), so `N ∈ Ncomp`. -/
theorem isToffoliPermGate_mem_deutschDataReachableCircuits {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α)
    (a₀ a₁ : Fin n) (ha : a₀ ≠ a₁) {N : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ}
    (hN : IsToffoliPermGate dataEnc N) :
    N ∈ deutschDataReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α := by
  obtain ⟨C, t, ht, hcard, rfl⟩ := hN
  obtain ⟨a, b, -, hC⟩ := exists_control_pair_descend_of_card_le_two e a₀ a₁ ha hcard
  have hSC : ∀ x : Fin m → Fin 2,
      (∀ k ∈ ({a, b} : Finset (Fin M)), regExtend e x k = 1) ↔ (∀ c ∈ C, x c = 1) :=
    fun x => forall_mem_regExtend_eq_one_iff e {a, b} C hC x
  have hcomp : compress (regEmbed fullEnc dataEnc e)
      (mcCtrlSingleQubit fullEnc {a, b} (e.symm (Sum.inl t)) pauliX)
        = permGate dataEnc (mcNotPerm C ht) := by
    rw [compress_mcCtrlSingleQubit_dataTarget_of_ctrl_iff fullEnc dataEnc e {a, b} t C pauliX hSC,
      mcCtrlSingleQubit_pauliX_eq_permGate dataEnc C ht]
  have hPmem : mcCtrlSingleQubit fullEnc {a, b} (e.symm (Sum.inl t)) pauliX
      ∈ deutschAncillaReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α := by
    apply Submonoid.subset_closure
    exact ⟨mcCtrlSingleQubit_dataTarget_mem_compressionInvariant fullEnc dataEnc e {a, b} t pauliX,
      a, b, e.symm (Sum.inl t),
      mcCtrlSingleQubit_pauliX_mem_closure_deutschWirePlacedReachable hα fullEnc a b
        (e.symm (Sum.inl t))⟩
  exact ⟨_, hPmem, hcomp⟩

/-- **Universality of the Deutsch gate `G = C²(iR_x(πα))` with ancillas, matrix level** (Nielsen &
Chuang, Exercise 4.44). When `α` is irrational and the data register has at least one qubit, for
*any* unitary `U ∈ U(2ⁿ)` some global phase `e^{ia}` makes `e^{ia} • U` a limit of
`deutschDataReachableCircuits` — the data-register actions of `G`-placement circuits with ancillas
held `|1⟩` are dense in `U(2ⁿ)` up to an (unobservable) global phase.

The abstract density core `exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschReachableCircuits` places
`e^{ia} • U` in the closure of `deutschReachableCircuits dataEnc α`, the circuits over the
*abstract* gate set `deutschReachableGateSet dataEnc α`. Both halves of that gate set are honest
compressed `G`-placements inside `Ncomp` — the single-qubit generators by
`singleQubitOnWire_mem_deutschDataReachableCircuits`, the reversible generators by
`isToffoliPermGate_mem_deutschDataReachableCircuits` — so
`deutschReachableCircuits dataEnc α ≤ Ncomp`
(`Submonoid.closure_le`) and hence `closure ↑(deutschReachableCircuits) ⊆ closure ↑Ncomp`
(`closure_mono`); transporting the density core along that containment gives the claim. -/
theorem exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschDataReachableCircuits [Nontrivial (Fin m → Fin 2)]
    {α : ℝ} (hα : Irrational α) (a₀ a₁ : Fin n) (ha : a₀ ≠ a₁)
    {U : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ} (hU : U ∈ Matrix.unitaryGroup (Fin d) ℂ) :
    ∃ a : ℝ, Complex.exp ((a : ℂ) * Complex.I) • U
      ∈ closure (↑(deutschDataReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α) :
        Set (Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ)) := by
  have hsub : deutschReachableGateSet dataEnc α
      ⊆ ↑(deutschDataReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α) := by
    rintro G (hG | hG)
    · exact isToffoliPermGate_mem_deutschDataReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e hα a₀ a₁ ha hG
    · rw [Set.mem_iUnion] at hG
      obtain ⟨j, g, hg, rfl⟩ := hG
      exact singleQubitOnWire_mem_deutschDataReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e hα a₀ a₁ ha j hg
  have hle : deutschReachableCircuits dataEnc α
      ≤ deutschDataReachableCircuits fullEnc dataEnc e α := Submonoid.closure_le.2 hsub
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := exists_phase_smul_mem_closure_deutschReachableCircuits hα dataEnc hU
  exact ⟨r, closure_mono (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.2 hle) hr⟩

end AxQM.Concrete
